   "daf": "113a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ קוֹשְׁרִין דְּלִי בְּפָסִקְיָא, אֲבָל לֹא בְּחֶבֶל. רַבִּי יְהוּדָה מַתִּיר. כְּלָל אָמַר רַבִּי יְהוּדָה: כׇּל קֶשֶׁר שֶׁאֵינוֹ שֶׁל קַיָּימָא — אֵין חַיָּיבִין עָלָיו.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «One may tie a bucket with a belt» on Shabbat, as he will certainly not leave it tied to the bucket, and therefore it is not a permanent knot. «But» one may «not» tie a bucket «with a rope. Rabbi Yehuda permits» doing so. «Rabbi Yehuda stated a principle:» With regard to «any knot that is not permanent, one is not liable» for tying «it.»"
  }
 ],
